note path-add, the command that does the real work. The parent step's file is indexed first, for the does-not-call note. The trailing numbers decide what was meant: none or one is a whole symbol, two or three is a line range, and the last number is the parent when it is there. Default parent is the last step added, so consecutive adds build a chain and an explicit index starts a branch.

